+# Proof/refutation frontier — S5-CLM-00003498
+
+The exact target is the even independent-domination assertion from
+`Arxiv.«2107.00295».independentDominationEven`:
+
+```text
+∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] (G : GraphData V),
+  0 < G.minDegree → Even G.maxDegree →
+  (G.maxDegree + 2)^2 * G.indepDominationNumber ≤
+    (G.maxDegree^2 + 4) * Fintype.card V
+```
+
+The source record is classified `research open` and contains `sorryAx`.  That
+source body is retained as metadata only; it is not proof evidence.
+
+## Checked boundary
+
+The Lean transport, a vacuous zero-minimum-degree boundary case, and one
+two-vertex numerical instance compile at trust level 0.  A positive-budget
+offline exploration checked 15 complete-graph parameter rows and 400 relaxed
+numeric rows.  The complete-graph rows all satisfy the inequality; 113 relaxed
+rows fail, which demonstrates why arbitrary numeric tuples cannot be promoted
+to graph counterexamples.
+
+## Open routes
+
+* Proof: derive a structural bound on independent domination in every finite
+  isolate-free graph and use the parity of the maximum degree.
+* Refutation: exhibit a realizable isolate-free even-degree graph violating the
+  bound, then prove its parameter values and a witness-to-negation bridge in
+  Lean.
+
+The four open cuts are `CUT-MAP-001`, `CUT-HUMAN-001`, `CUT-MACHINE-001`, and
+`CUT-READABLE-001`.  Consequently `RES-ROOT-OPEN` is not a terminal proof or
+refutation node, and the canonical Master must keep the TARGET at underscore.
