+# Human resolution record
+
+## Decision
+
+No complete proof or refutation of the exact even independent-domination
+conjecture was found in this run.  The mathematically honest outcome is
+**open**.  This is a negative resolution receipt, not a claim that the
+conjecture is false.
+
+The exact target is the statement recorded as
+`Arxiv.«2107.00295».independentDominationEven`, with Claim fingerprint
+`bbfc9ecaca2c50de4f3a8d8ab32fd1640351f5946b8790bbc1e9894c952e46b4` and
+resolution root `RES-ROOT-OPEN`.
+
+The source is marked `research open` and its `sorryAx` body is not used as
+evidence.  The target-local Lean package checks the proposition transport, a
+vacuous zero-minimum-degree boundary, and a finite two-vertex numerical
+instance.  Those checks establish only local consistency.
+
+## Exploration interpretation
+
+The first offline command examined 400 relaxed tuples of even degree,
+independent number, and order subject to `i ≤ n`; 287 satisfy the arithmetic
+inequality and 113 fail.  Because those tuples are not certified graph
+invariants, the failures are diagnostics rather than counterexamples.  The
+second command checked 15 complete-graph parameter rows (`K_n`, `n ≤ 32`, even
+maximum degree), all of which satisfy the bound.  One graph family cannot settle
+the universal assertion.
+
+## Missing mathematical bridge
+
+A proof needs a structural theorem controlling independent domination in every
+finite isolate-free graph and using evenness of the maximum degree to obtain the
+stated coefficient.  A refutation needs a realizable graph with even maximum
+degree that violates the inequality, together with a formal witness-to-negation
+argument.  Neither bridge is present.
+
+## Review and release boundary
+
+The candidate DAG therefore keeps `RES-ROOT-OPEN` open with nonempty mapping,
+human, machine, and readability cuts.  No independent reviewer has accepted a
+proof or counterexample, and no canonical Master resolve event exists.  The
+appropriate handoff is
+`exploration_package_accepted_pending_resolution`; the TARGET remains
+unfinished and must not transition from underscore to x.
