+# Resolution outline
+
+This is a route map for the open target, not a completed proof.
+
+## Exact root
+
+`R0` is `Arxiv.«2107.00295».Claim`, with Claim polarity and statement digest
+`bbfc9ecaca2c50de4f3a8d8ab32fd1640351f5946b8790bbc1e9894c952e46b4`.
+
+## Candidate proof route
+
+1. Establish the exact graph-theoretic definition and basic inequalities for
+   independent domination.
+2. Relate the number of vertices covered by a minimum independent dominating
+   set to the even maximum degree.
+3. Sum the local counting inequalities to obtain
+   `(D + 2)^2 * i ≤ (D^2 + 4) * n`.
+4. Compose the argument in Lean with the exact source polarity and inspect all
+   transitive axioms.
+
+The checked two-vertex case is only a base sanity anchor; it does not supply
+step 2 for arbitrary graphs.
+
+## Candidate refutation route
+
+1. Search even-regular, bipartite, and near-regular isolate-free graph
+   families beyond complete graphs.
+2. Compute `D`, `i(G)`, and `n` from the source definitions, not a numeric
+   surrogate.
+3. If the inequality fails, formalize the graph and a strict inequality to
+   derive `Not Claim`.
+
+No realizable counterexample was found in the bounded worker search.
+
+## Required gates
+
+An accepted result needs an exact human argument, a placeholder-free theorem at
+the exact polarity, an immutable reviewed DAG, injective readable anchors, and
+cold offline replay.  Until then `CUT-MAP-001`, `CUT-HUMAN-001`,
+`CUT-MACHINE-001`, and `CUT-READABLE-001` remain open.
