+type.  `Audit.lean` prints the declarations and their foundation axioms.
+
+## 4. Exploration
+
+`research/attempt-001.json` records two offline positive-budget commands.  A
+relaxed box of 400 numerical tuples has 113 violations, proving only that
+numeric tuples cannot stand in for realizable graph invariants.  A complete-
+graph family search for 15 rows with `n ≤ 32` and even maximum degree has no
+violations.  These bounded observations guide routes but do not settle the
+universal quantifier.
+
+## 5. Proof/refutation frontier
+
+The proof route needs a structural independent-domination bound with the parity
+sharpening in the conjecture.  The refutation route needs an actual
+isolate-free even-degree graph violating the inequality and a formal bridge to
+`Not Claim`.  The current DAG records both routes and leaves all four required
+cuts open.
+
+## 6. Resolution and machine state
+
+Resolution proof units version 1 is an immutable candidate rooted at
+`RES-ROOT-OPEN` with Claim polarity.  Its mapping, candidate-human,
+candidate-machine, and readability cut sets are nonempty.  Machine closure is
+false: no exact root theorem is declared.  Human resolution is likewise open.
+
+## 7. Reproducibility and invalidation
+
+The package records source, baseline, provider, Stage6, command, output, and
+artifact bindings.  A source or proposition change, parity/premise mutation,
+provider migration, or changed Stage6 alias invalidates the handoff.  A future
+proof or counterexample must stay under this TARGET, use a strictly increasing
+DAG version, and preserve version 1 in immutable history.
+
+## 8. Handoff conclusion
+
+The target-local INTAKE, STATEMENT, STATUS, FRONTIER, EXPLORE, RESOLUTION,
+HUMAN, LEAN, READABLE, VALIDATE, and RELEASE surfaces are populated for
+canonical review.  The exact conjecture remains open, so this package is a
+provisional exploration handoff and not an underscore-to-x completion.
